{
  "description": "Contacts, their segments, topics and imports. Live responses (2026-10-29), matching resend-node: deleteContact returns the contact id as `contact`, not `id`. Adding a contact to a segment returns `{ id, audienceId }` and removing one returns `{ object, id, audienceId, deleted }`, where `id` is the contact and `audienceId` (camelCase on the wire) the segment; the spec's `contact_id` and `segment_id` never appear. listContactTopics items carry `created_at`. updateContactTopics takes the topic list as the bare JSON body, as resend-node sends it (the spec's `{ topics: [...] }` is refused with 422), and answers `{ object, id }` with the contact id. `audience_id` is removed from createContact, where `segment_id` replaces it. Response members are narrowed to what Resend returns: required where resend-node, the maintained official SDK, declares them non-optional and every live response (2026-10-29) carried them, and nullable where resend-node allows null or a live response held null. Errors on these operations match Resend's error `name` and status; the classes shared with other areas are in shared.json.",
